  "details": "Sometimes when the controllers seem to go inactive, vrchat snaps your avatar's arms down to your sides. However, I can tell that the controllers have not actually gone inactive, because my steamVR wrist overlay still remains in the correct position. Even the little indicator in vrc that says one handed movement remains in the correct position, while the avatar's hand visibly snaps down to my side.\n\nObviously, part of the problem is the oculus firmware putting the controllers to sleep too quickly. But it seems as though vrchat exacerbates this issue by snapping your arms down before the controllers even actually stop reporting position.\n\nPlaying the steamvr build on a quest pro with pro controllers through virtual desktop.",
